&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Backend Engineer to join our Repository Management team within GitLab&#39;s Source Code stage. You&#39;ll help customers configure repositories with confidence so their GitLab projects support the way their teams work. As artificial intelligence agents increasingly write and manage code alongside people, you&#39;ll build guardrails that make development safe and trustworthy. You&#39;ll turn complex policy and repository management needs into reliable backend solutions that support people and the agents working on their behalf.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work in one of GitLab&#39;s oldest and most complex product areas, using Ruby and GraphQL to improve a critical system that serves GitLab.com, self-managed instances, and GitLab Dedicated. Source Code provides the interface layer, through Gitaly, to the Git repositories that account for a large portion of GitLab traffic. With support from experienced team members, you&#39;ll help maintain high reliability through performance and structured query language tuning, caching, rate limiting, testing, observability, and resiliency. You&#39;ll collaborate with product management, product design, testing, security, user experience research, technical writing, Gitaly, Code Review, and Source Code Experience to deliver reliable and performant systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learn more about the &lt;a class=&quot;textLink&quot; href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/engineering/devops/create/source-code/&quot;&gt;Create:Source Code teams&lt;/a&gt; in the GitLab Handbook.&lt;/p&gt;
